This chapter shares only advance and resolve.

Use the foundation, maps, battle, pack, party, commands, lettering and sound chapters.

A storybook has a scene (text), a challenger (text), a gym trainer beaten (number), a forest one beaten (number), a forest two beaten (number) and a forest three beaten (number) and a grass steps (number) and a route rival beaten (number) and a recovery place (text).
There is a storybook called Story whose scene is "" and whose challenger is "" and whose gym trainer beaten is 0 and whose forest one beaten is 0 and whose forest two beaten is 0 and whose forest three beaten is 0 and whose grass steps is 0 and whose route rival beaten is 0 and whose recovery place is "Home".

The dialogue transitions are next scene and dialogue, in that order:
  "oak warning" has "oak lab" and "OAK: Come with me!".
  "brock cash" has "brock badge" and "BROCK: I took you for granted. As proof of your victory, here's the BOULDERBADGE!".
  "brock advice" has "brock tm" and "That's an official POKEMON LEAGUE BADGE! Its bearer's POKEMON become more powerful! The technique FLASH can now be used any time!".
  "brock tm" has "brock tm received" and "Wait! Take this with you!".
  "brock explanation" has "" and "A TM contains a technique that can be taught to POKEMON! A TM is good only once! TM34 contains BIDE! Your POKEMON will absorb damage in battle then pay it back double!".

The challenge opponents are challenger, in that order:
  "rival challenge" has "rival".
  "brock challenge" has "brock".
  "route rival challenge" has "route rival".

The starter pairs are chosen starter and chosen rival starter, in that order:
  "0" has "Bulbasaur" and "Charmander".
  "1" has "Charmander" and "Squirtle".
  "2" has "Squirtle" and "Bulbasaur".

The parting words are victory line and defeat line, in that order:
  "wild" has "The wild POKEMON fainted!" and "".
  "rival" has "RIVAL: WHAT? Unbelievable! I picked the wrong POKEMON!" and "RIVAL: Yeah! Am I great or what?".
  "route rival" has "RIVAL: What? I was just careless!" and "RIVAL: You have to work harder than that!".
  "gym trainer" has "GYM TRAINER: Darn! Light years isn't time, it measures distance!" and "".
  "forest one" has "BUG CATCHER: You're a POKEMON trainer too!" and "".
  "forest two" has "BUG CATCHER: I give up! You're good at this!" and "".
  "forest three" has "BUG CATCHER: No! Caterpie can't hack it!" and "".

The forest bouts are challenger and challenge, in that order:
  "Bug Catcher 1" has "forest one" and "BUG CATCHER: Hey! You have POKEMON! Come on! Let's battle 'em!".
  "Bug Catcher 2" has "forest two" and "BUG CATCHER: Yo! You can't jam out if you're a POKEMON trainer!".
  "Bug Catcher 3" has "forest three" and "BUG CATCHER: Hey, wait up! What's the hurry?".

The recovery spots are column and row, in that order:
  "Home" has 2 and 6.
  "Viridian Center" has 3 and 6.
  "Pewter Center" has 3 and 6.

Let the brock prize always be 99 * 14.
Let the opening length always be 144.
Let the naming width always be 6.
Let the naming cells always be 30.
Let the letter cells always be 26.
Let the erase cell always be 28.
Let the done cell always be 29.
Let the inscription limit always be 7.

To speak a line (text):
  Set Journey's message to the line.
  Set Journey's mode to dialogue.

To engage:
  Challenge Story's challenger.
  Reset Orders.
  Set Journey's mode to battle.

To finish:
  Let the transition be the dialogue transitions for Story's scene.
  If the transition is not nothing:
    Set Story's scene to the transition's next scene.
    Speak the transition's dialogue.
    Stop.
  Depending on Story's scene:
    For "mart parcel":
      Set Story's scene to "".
      Set Journey's column to 2.
      Set Journey's row to 4.
      Set Journey's facing to "north".
      Set Journey's parcel to 1.
      Sound "item".
      Set Journey's objective to "Deliver OAK's PARCEL to his lab in PALLET TOWN.".
      Speak "CLERK: You know PROF. OAK, right? His order came in. Will you take it to him? You got OAK's PARCEL!".
    For "oak lab":
      Set Story's scene to "".
      Set Journey's place to "Oak's Lab".
      Set Journey's column to 5.
      Set Journey's row to 4.
      Set Journey's facing to "north".
      Set Journey's stage to "choose starter".
      Set Journey's objective to "Choose a Pokemon from Oak's table.".
      Speak "OAK: There are 3 POKEMON here! Choose one!".
    For "starter chosen":
      Set Story's scene to "".
      Speak "{Journey's rival}: I'll take this one, then! {Journey's rival} received {Journey's rival starter}!".
    For "brock badge":
      Set Story's scene to "brock advice".
      Sound "badge".
      Speak "{Journey's trainer} received the BOULDERBADGE!".
    For "brock tm received":
      Set Journey's tm34 to 1.
      Set Journey's objective to "Brock awarded you the Boulder Badge and TM34.".
      Set Story's scene to "brock explanation".
      Sound "item".
      Speak "{Journey's trainer} received TM34!".
    For "deliver parcel":
      Set Story's scene to "".
      Set Journey's parcel to 0.
      Set Journey's dex to 1.
      Set Journey's stage to "pokedex".
      Set Journey's objective to "Travel through Viridian Forest to Pewter Gym.".
      Speak "OAK: This is my invention, POKEDEX! It automatically records data on POKEMON you've seen or caught!".
    For "trainer challenge":
      Set Story's scene to "".
      Engage.
    Otherwise:
      Let the opponent be the challenge opponents for Story's scene.
      If the opponent is not nothing:
        Set Story's scene to "".
        Set Story's challenger to the opponent's challenger.
        Engage.
      Otherwise:
        Set Story's scene to "".
        Set Journey's mode to walk.
        Set Journey's message to "".

To decline:
  Set Journey's mode to walk.
  Set Journey's message to "".

To choose:
  Let the pair be the starter pairs for "{Journey's selection}".
  If the pair is nothing:
    Decline.
    Stop.
  Set Journey's starter to the pair's chosen starter.
  Set Journey's rival starter to the pair's chosen rival starter.
  Enlist Journey's starter.
  Set Journey's stage to "rival battle".
  Set Story's scene to "starter chosen".
  Speak "OAK: This POKEMON is really energetic! {Journey's trainer} received {Journey's starter}!".

To beat a challenger (text):
  Depending on the challenger:
    For "route rival":
      Set Story's route rival beaten to 1.
      Set Journey's route rival beaten to 1.
    For "gym trainer":
      Set Story's gym trainer beaten to 1.
    For "forest one":
      Set Story's forest one beaten to 1.
    For "forest two":
      Set Story's forest two beaten to 1.
    For "forest three":
      Set Story's forest three beaten to 1.
    For "brock":
      If Journey's badge is 0:
        Set Journey's badge to 1.
        Add the brock prize to Journey's wallet.
        Set Journey's stage to "boulder badge".
        Set Journey's objective to "Receive the BOULDERBADGE and TM34 from BROCK.".
        Set Story's scene to "brock cash".
        Speak "{Journey's trainer} got {the brock prize} for winning!".
      Stop.
  Let the parting be the parting words for the challenger.
  If the parting is not nothing:
    Speak the parting's victory line.

To recover:
  Revive.
  Set Journey's wallet to (Journey's wallet / 2) rounded down to the nearest 1.
  Set Journey's place to Story's recovery place.
  Let the spot be the recovery spots for Story's recovery place.
  If the spot is not nothing:
    Set Journey's column to the spot's column.
    Set Journey's row to the spot's row.
  Set Journey's facing to "north".

To lose to a challenger (text):
  Let the parting be the parting words for the challenger.
  Let the taunt be the parting's defeat line or else "".
  If the challenger is "rival":
    Speak the taunt.
    Stop.
  Recover.
  Let the blackout be "{Journey's trainer} is out of usable POKEMON! {Journey's trainer} blacked out!".
  If the taunt is "":
    Speak the blackout.
  Otherwise:
    Speak "{the taunt} {the blackout}".

To resolve:
  If Combat's outcome is "" or Combat is reporting:
    Stop.
  If Combat's outcome is "fainted":
    Replace.
    If Combat's outcome is "":
      Stop.
  If Combat's outcome is one of "escaped" or "caught":
    Set Combat's outcome to "".
    Set Story's challenger to "".
    Set Journey's mode to walk.
    Stop.
  If Story's challenger is "rival":
    Set Journey's stage to "parcel".
    Set Journey's objective to "Visit the Viridian City MART.".
  Depending on Combat's outcome:
    For "win":
      Beat Story's challenger.
    For "loss":
      Lose to Story's challenger.
  Set Combat's outcome to "".
  Set Story's challenger to "".

To work out the defeats (number) of a challenger (text):
  Choose the answer by the challenger:
    For "forest one", use Story's forest one beaten.
    For "forest two", use Story's forest two beaten.
    For "forest three", use Story's forest three beaten.
    Otherwise, use 0.

To work out the starter slot (number) of a species (text):
  Choose the answer by the species:
    For "Charmander", use 1.
    For "Squirtle", use 2.
    Otherwise, use 0.

To meet a visitor (text):
  Depending on the visitor:
    For "Oak":
      If Journey's stage is "choose starter":
        Speak "OAK: Go on! Choose a POKEMON!".
      Otherwise if Journey's parcel is 1 and Journey's dex is 0:
        Set Story's scene to "deliver parcel".
        Speak "OAK: Ah! This is the custom POKE BALL I ordered! Thank you!".
      Otherwise if Journey's dex is 1:
        Speak "OAK: You can't get detailed data on POKEMON by just seeing them. You must catch them!".
      Otherwise:
        Speak "OAK: How is my old POKEMON? Go to VIRIDIAN CITY for me.".
    For "Bulbasaur", "Charmander" or "Squirtle":
      If Journey's stage is "choose starter":
        Set Journey's selection to the starter slot of the visitor.
        Set Journey's mode to starter.
        Set Journey's message to "Choose {the visitor}? A: yes  B: no".
      Otherwise:
        Speak "OAK: Don't be greedy!".
    For "Route 22 Rival":
      If Story's route rival beaten is 1 or Journey's badge is 1:
        Speak "RIVAL: Smell ya later!".
      Otherwise:
        Set Story's scene to "route rival challenge".
        Speak "RIVAL: Hey! You're going to POKEMON LEAGUE? Forget it! You probably don't have any BADGES!".
    For "Rival":
      Speak "RIVAL: Smell ya later!".
    For "Nurse":
      Set Story's recovery place to Journey's place.
      Revive.
      Sound "heal".
      Speak "NURSE: We've healed your POKEMON back to perfect health!".
    For "Daisy":
      If Journey's town map is 1:
        Speak "DAISY: Use the TOWN MAP to find out where you are.".
      Otherwise if Journey's dex is 1:
        Set Journey's town map to 1.
        Sound "item".
        Speak "DAISY: This will help you! {Journey's trainer} got a TOWN MAP!".
      Otherwise:
        Speak "DAISY: My brother is at Grandpa's lab.".
    For "Mom":
      Revive.
      Speak "MOM: Right. All boys leave home someday. It said so on TV. OAK, next door, is looking for you.".
    For "Clerk":
      If Journey's stage is "parcel" and Journey's parcel is 0 and Journey's dex is 0:
        Set Journey's parcel to 1.
        Sound "item".
        Set Journey's objective to "Deliver OAK's PARCEL to his lab in PALLET TOWN.".
        Speak "CLERK: You came from PALLET TOWN? Please take OAK's PARCEL to him!".
      Otherwise if Journey's dex is 0:
        Speak "CLERK: Say hi to PROFESSOR OAK for me!".
      Otherwise:
        Set Journey's mode to shop.
        Set Journey's message to "CLERK: Welcome!".
    For "Brock":
      If Journey's badge is 1:
        Speak "BROCK: There are all kinds of trainers in the world!".
      Otherwise:
        Set Story's scene to "brock challenge".
        Speak "I'm BROCK! I'm PEWTER's GYM LEADER! I believe in rock hard defense and determination! That's why my POKEMON are all the rock-type! Do you still want to challenge me? Fine then! Show me your best!".
    For "Gym Trainer":
      If Story's gym trainer beaten is 1 or Journey's badge is 1:
        Speak "GYM TRAINER: Light years measures distance!".
      Otherwise:
        Set Story's scene to "trainer challenge".
        Set Story's challenger to "gym trainer".
        Speak "Stop right there, kid! You're 10,000 light years from facing BROCK!".
    For "Bug Catcher 1", "Bug Catcher 2" or "Bug Catcher 3":
      Let the bout be the forest bouts for the visitor.
      If the bout is not nothing and the defeats of the bout's challenger is 0:
        Set Story's scene to "trainer challenge".
        Set Story's challenger to the bout's challenger.
        Speak the bout's challenge.
      Otherwise:
        Speak "Hello! Good luck on your journey!".
    Otherwise:
      If the visitor is not "":
        Speak "Hello! Good luck on your journey!".

To return to a place (text) at a column (number) by a row (number):
  Set Journey's place to the place.
  Set Journey's column to the column.
  Set Journey's row to the row.

To walk toward a direction (text):
  Let the old place be Journey's place.
  Let the old column be Journey's column.
  Let the old row be Journey's row.
  Travel the direction.
  If Journey's place is "Pallet Town" and the old place is not "Pallet Town" and Journey's town map is 1 and Journey's blue house entered is 1:
    Set Journey's daisy walking to 1.
  If Journey's place is "Blue's House" and the old place is not "Blue's House":
    Set Journey's blue house entered to 1.
  If the old place is "Oak's Lab" and Journey's place is "Pallet Town" and Journey's stage is "choose starter":
    Return to the old place at the old column by the old row.
    Speak "OAK: Hey! Don't go away yet!".
    Stop.
  If the old place is "Oak's Lab" and Journey's place is "Pallet Town" and Journey's stage is "rival battle":
    Return to the old place at the old column by the old row.
    Set Story's scene to "rival challenge".
    Speak "{Journey's rival}: Wait {Journey's trainer}! Let's check out our POKEMON! Come on, I'll take you on!".
    Stop.
  If the old place is "Viridian City" and Journey's place is "Viridian Mart" and Journey's stage is "parcel" and Journey's parcel is 0 and Journey's dex is 0:
    Set Story's scene to "mart parcel".
    Speak "CLERK: Hey! You came from PALLET TOWN?".
    Stop.
  If Journey's place is "Route 1" and Journey's starter is "":
    Return to the old place at the old column by the old row.
    Set Story's scene to "oak warning".
    Speak "OAK: Hey! Wait! Don't go out! It's unsafe! Wild POKEMON live in tall grass!".
    Stop.
  If Journey's place is "Route 2" and Journey's dex is 0:
    Return to the old place at the old column by the old row.
    Speak "The road is closed. First help PROFESSOR OAK with his parcel.".
    Stop.
  If Journey's place is "Viridian Forest" and (Journey's column is not the old column or Journey's row is not the old row):
    If Journey's row is 33 and Journey's column is at least 26 and Journey's column is less than 30 and Story's forest one beaten is 0:
      Meet "Bug Catcher 1".
      Stop.
    If Journey's row is 19 and Journey's column is at least 26 and Journey's column is less than 30 and Story's forest two beaten is 0:
      Meet "Bug Catcher 2".
      Stop.
    If Journey's row is 18 and Journey's column is 1 and Story's forest three beaten is 0:
      Meet "Bug Catcher 3".
      Stop.
  If Journey's starter is not "" and the terrain at Journey's column by Journey's row is "grass":
    If Journey's column is not the old column or Journey's row is not the old row or Journey's place is not the old place:
      Add 1 to Story's grass steps.
      If Story's grass steps is at least 8:
        Set Story's grass steps to 0.
        Set Story's challenger to "wild".
        Encounter Journey's place.
        Reset Orders.
        Set Journey's mode to battle.

To nominate:
  Set Journey's selection to 0.
  Set Journey's mode to rival naming.
  Set Journey's message to "OAK: This is my grandson. What was his name?".

To begin:
  Set Journey's place to "Bedroom".
  Set Journey's column to 3.
  Set Journey's row to 6.
  Set Journey's facing to "north".
  Set Journey's stage to "find oak".
  Set Journey's objective to "Find PROFESSOR OAK in PALLET TOWN.".
  Set Journey's mode to walk.
  Set Journey's message to "".

To enter a key (text):
  If the key is "left":
    Subtract 1 from Journey's selection.
    If Journey's selection is less than 0:
      Set Journey's selection to the done cell.
  If the key is "right":
    Add 1 to Journey's selection.
    If Journey's selection is more than the done cell:
      Set Journey's selection to 0.
  If the key is "up":
    Subtract the naming width from Journey's selection.
    If Journey's selection is less than 0:
      Add the naming cells to Journey's selection.
  If the key is "down":
    Add the naming width to Journey's selection.
    If Journey's selection is at least the naming cells:
      Subtract the naming cells from Journey's selection.
  Let the inscription be Journey's trainer.
  If Journey's mode is custom rival naming:
    Set the inscription to Journey's rival.
  If the key is "b" or (the key is "a" and Journey's selection is the erase cell):
    If the length of the inscription is more than 0:
      Set the inscription to the first (the length of the inscription - 1) letters of the inscription.
  If the key is "a" and Journey's selection is less than the letter cells and the length of the inscription is less than the inscription limit:
    Let the letter be letter (Journey's selection + 1) of "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ" or else "".
    Set the inscription to "{the inscription}{the letter}".
  If Journey's mode is custom naming:
    Set Journey's trainer to the inscription.
  Otherwise:
    Set Journey's rival to the inscription.
  If the key is "start" or (the key is "a" and Journey's selection is the done cell):
    If the inscription is not "":
      If Journey's mode is custom naming:
        Nominate.
      Otherwise:
        Begin.

To direct with a key (text):
  Command the key.
  Resolve.

To unveil with a key (text):
  If (the key is one of "start" or "a") or Journey's animation is at least the opening length:
    Set Journey's mode to title.
    Set Journey's animation to 0.

To dismiss with a key (text):
  If the key is one of "start" or "a":
    Set Journey's mode to main menu.

To embark with a key (text):
  If the key is one of "start" or "a":
    Set Journey's mode to intro.
    Set Journey's selection to 0.
    Set Journey's message to "OAK: Hello there! Welcome to the world of POKEMON! My name is OAK! People call me the POKEMON PROF!".

To introduce with a key (text):
  If the key is one of "a" or "start":
    Let the intro remainder be the caption remainder for Journey's message.
    If the intro remainder is not "":
      Set Journey's message to the intro remainder.
      Stop.
    If Journey's selection is 0:
      Set Journey's selection to 1.
      Set Journey's message to "OAK: This world is inhabited by creatures called POKEMON! For some people, POKEMON are pets. Others use them for fights.".
    Otherwise:
      Set Journey's selection to 0.
      Set Journey's mode to naming.
      Set Journey's message to "OAK: First, what is your name? Choose a name.".

To designate with a key (text):
  If the key is one of "up" or "left":
    Subtract 1 from Journey's selection.
    If Journey's selection is less than 0:
      Set Journey's selection to 3.
  If the key is one of "down" or "right":
    Add 1 to Journey's selection.
    If Journey's selection is more than 3:
      Set Journey's selection to 0.
  If the key is one of "a" or "start":
    If Journey's mode is naming:
      If Journey's selection is 0:
        Set Journey's trainer to "".
        Set Journey's mode to custom naming.
        Stop.
      Set Journey's trainer to "RED".
      If Journey's selection is 2:
        Set Journey's trainer to "ASH".
      If Journey's selection is 3:
        Set Journey's trainer to "JACK".
      Nominate.
    Otherwise:
      If Journey's selection is 0:
        Set Journey's rival to "".
        Set Journey's mode to custom rival naming.
        Stop.
      Set Journey's rival to "BLUE".
      If Journey's selection is 2:
        Set Journey's rival to "GARY".
      If Journey's selection is 3:
        Set Journey's rival to "JOHN".
      Begin.

To page with a key (text):
  If the key is one of "a", "b" or "start":
    Let the remainder be the caption remainder for Journey's message.
    If the remainder is not "":
      Set Journey's message to the remainder.
    Otherwise:
      Finish.

To adopt with a key (text):
  If the key is "a":
    Choose.
  If the key is "b":
    Decline.

To explore with a key (text):
  If the key is one of "up", "down", "left" or "right":
    Walk toward the key.
  If the key is "a":
    If Journey's place is "Bedroom" and Journey's row is 2 and Journey's column is 3 and Journey's facing is "north" and "PC Potion" is not in Stock's found:
      Add "PC Potion" to Stock's found.
      Add 1 to Stock's potions.
      Sound "item".
      Speak "Withdrew a POTION from the PC!".
    Otherwise:
      If the person ahead is not "":
        Meet the person ahead.
      Otherwise:
        Examine.

To advance a key (text):
  Depending on Journey's mode:
    For battle:
      Direct with the key.
    For opening:
      Unveil with the key.
    For title:
      Dismiss with the key.
    For main menu:
      Embark with the key.
    For intro:
      Introduce with the key.
    For naming or rival naming:
      Designate with the key.
    For custom naming or custom rival naming:
      Enter the key.
    For dialogue:
      Page with the key.
    For starter:
      Adopt with the key.
    For walk:
      Explore with the key.
